    "problem_statement": "Horizontal Rule Rendering Issue with Markdown and Random Styles\n\nDescription\n\nIt seems there's a problem with how horizontal rules are rendered in tables when using certain styles, specifically \"MARKDOWN\" and \"RANDOM\". The issue appears to affect the alignment and junction characters, leading to unexpected table formatting.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Create a table using the PrettyTable library.\n2. Set the table style to \"MARKDOWN\" or \"RANDOM\".\n3. Add a few rows and columns with data.\n4. Render the table and observe the horizontal rules and junctions.\n\nExpected behavior:\nThe table should render with correctly aligned horizontal rules and junction characters according to the specified style.\n\nActual behavior:\nThe horizontal rules and junction characters are misaligned or incorrect, causing the table to appear malformed.\n\nThis issue is particularly noticeable when using the \"MARKDOWN\" style, where the alignment characters do not match the expected output. Similarly, the \"RANDOM\" style exhibits unexpected characters in the table rendering.\n\nThis behavior was observed in the latest version of the library. Please investigate and address this rendering inconsistency."
  },
